A||N||8||Jefrysuko||Rodney Dickman's exhaust hangers||||1||
Z||000000||Jefrysuko||12-30-2001||11:49 PM||||The week before Christmas Rodney made a trip down to my house to borrow the exhaust off my 88 GT.  He needed my exhaust so that he could take measurements for the manufacturing of his aftermarket exhaust.  To thank me for letting him borrow my exhaust he sent me a set of his exhaust hangers.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.rodneydickman.com/exhausthanger1.jpg"> <BR>These hangers are of exceptional quality and if GM would have made the originals this way they would have lasted the life of the car.<P>The original hangers were made of mild steal and required plenty of liquid wrench in order to get them off.  Rodney makes his out of stainless steal so that should not be a problem with these.  Rodney also used a heavier duty clamp which should be beneficial also.  Another thing that I noticed is that Rodney welded the bracket to the top of the clamp so that you don't crush your pipe when you tighten down the clamp.  It even appears as if he had the upper bracket laser cut to look just like the original.<P>While I was talking to Rodney he mentioned to me that he even had special U-bolts made for him because he wasn't satisfied with anything that he had found.  The set he sent me was one of his prototypes which I think will have about 6-7 threads showing on the bolts (as in the picture above) where as the originals showed 2-3 threads.  According to Rodney the U-bolts he had made will only show 2-3 threads like the originals.<P>I am always amazed by the amount of effort that Rodney puts into everything that he makes and these hangers are no exception.  I am now anxiously awaiting the release of his exhaust system and am saving my money so that I can buy one, and another set of hangers, for my SE.<P>For those of you that like pictures I will post some of these hangers and many of the other products that I have bought from Rodney over the years later in the week when I get them back from the developers.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-31-2001||12:31 AM||||I too am awaiting Rodney's exhaust.  I hope he will start selling the coupe tips too in polished stainless steel too.  The exhaust system I am putting in my coupe in the spring when I put in the V6 will retain the stock, coupe-style tips becuase I like the look.  Mine are all rusted and crappy, and I think polished stainless would look great.  I don't like chrome though, too shiney and flashy.<P>All of Rodney's products are great.  His effort definatly shows and I resent the Fiero Store for being pansies and buying his products to copy them, instead of doing their own freakin research.<P>Keep it up Rodney!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierojoesig2.gif">  <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||yo_sweet||12-31-2001||01:54 AM||||why is it that on most fiero's the right exausht tip always hangs lower "stock" that is, do they move or sink? the lefty seems always to be higher and never level<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rearviewgta_1_2_1.jpg">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000003||blayde8||12-31-2001||02:13 AM||||Sweet to hear the good news, I need some hangers.  And of course I'll order from Rodney! I've only heard good about him!||||reg||7
Z||000004||fropuff||12-31-2001||10:46 AM||||Those look nice!  I'm thinking about taking my old crappy ones out and putting those in place.  I have to replace the right side one anyway.  I guess they tend to snap when you get run over by a frickin van; I heard this somewhere.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Maybe it'll fix the uneven exhaust as well.  I'll have to keep an eye out for them..||||reg||1
Z||000005||KissMySSFiero||12-31-2001||10:49 AM||||RODNEY DOES IT AGAIN!!!!!!<BR>HOW COME HES ALWAYS GETTING THESE PLUGS FROM VERY SATISFIED CUSTOMERS?  OH WAIT HE'S JUST THAT GOOD.   <BR>sorry for yelling.  Im going to drive my fiero now.  been over 2 weeks.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>Two 88FORMULAS Red & Yellow<BR>        <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>         <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000006||Jefrysuko||12-31-2001||11:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>why is it that on most fiero's the right exausht tip always hangs lower "stock" that is, do they move or sink? the lefty seems always to be higher and never level<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I have seen several cars that had hangers that actually rusted through and since the main weight of the exhaust system is on the right side, the right side hangs lower and the left is higher.  Basically you are just seeing lazy people that need to get a set of Rodney's hangers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jefrysuko||12-31-2001||11:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>I too am awaiting Rodney's exhaust.  I hope he will start selling the coupe tips too in polished stainless steel too.  The exhaust system I am putting in my coupe in the spring when I put in the V6 will retain the stock, coupe-style tips becuase I like the look.  Mine are all rusted and crappy, and I think polished stainless would look great.  I don't like chrome though, too shiney and flashy.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>From what Rodney told me about his exhaust he is planning on making it out of 304 stainless which is the same material as the factory exhaust.  I don't think you can polish 304 and have it stay shinny for any length of time.  So in order to do what you are saying it would have to be made out of a higher grade stainless.  If this is really what you are looking for, and think others are looking for the same, I would let Rodney know.  I talked to him for quite some time the day he was down here and then again a couple days later about his exhaust.  He gets a lot of ideas from people that spend the time to tell him about them.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierokid87||12-31-2001||12:59 PM||||I am plannign to get these hangers as well as his vacume lines and acouple other things.  Im glad Radney is in the Fiero community.  He is a big help to everyone.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
